"""Standalone, install-free verifier for an underwrite export bundle.

Run it directly against a bundle tar -- it needs ONLY the Python 3.12+
standard library: no underwrite install, no third-party packages, no
network.

    python -I verify.py BUNDLE.tar [--expected-roles r1,r2,...] [--json]

What it independently re-verifies (CONTENT INTEGRITY / tamper-evidence):
  1. every blob's sha256 matches its own blobs/sha256/<hex> path and the
     BagIt manifest (manifest-sha256.txt),
  2. index.json declares every REQUIRED role -- the required set is fixed
     by --expected-roles (default "receipt"), never read as a default FROM
     index.json itself, so dropping a blob, its manifest line, AND its
     index descriptor together still fails closed with MISSING_ROLE,
  3. if index.json declares a "ledger_chain" role, its rows form a
     correctly hashed, contiguous append-only chain; if it also declares
     an "anchor" role, the chain's head is pinned to that anchor,
  4. any tar member with an absolute path or a ".." segment is rejected
     outright (UNSAFE_PATH) before anything is extracted.

What it deliberately does NOT assert: issuer
AUTHENTICITY. Signature verification is a separate, optional step
("verify --signatures", not implemented by this stdlib-only script) --
this script catches CONTENT and CHAIN tampering, which is what standard
tooling can confirm without any secret key.

Generated by gen_verify.py from underwrite_core.{canonical,chain,bundle} so
its exact source can be shipped inside every bundle -- see
tests/unit/pure/test_verify_parity.py (behavior parity) and
tests/unit/pure/test_verify_generated_drift.py (no drift).
"""


